Under Model A Integrated PhDs in Essex Business School (BE1.0), to pass Year One (the Postgraduate Taught phase) and proceed to Year Two, a student must:

a) Attempt 180 credits at Masters level (level 7), of which at least 140 must be passed, with any remaining credits condoned, subject to (c);

b) Pass all taught core modules with a mark of 60 or more in each taught core module;

c) Failure with a mark of 40–49 for up to 40 credits in non-core taught modules may be condoned.

Source: https://www.essex.ac.uk/-/media/documents/directories/academic-section/rules-of-assessment/pgt/2025-26/other-pgt-awards/integrated-phd-variations-model-a-25.pdf
